{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And the man called.</b> Scripture returned to its earlier matter — 'and the man called names' — and interrupted only to teach you that through the calling of names Eve was paired with him, as written: 'but for Adam He did not find a helper corresponding to him' — therefore 'and He caused a deep sleep to fall.' And because it wrote 'and they were naked,' it juxtaposed the section of the serpent, to inform you that from the fact that it saw her nakedness and saw them engaged in intercourse, it desired her and came upon them with scheming and deceit." "<b>Eve.</b> It falls under the root חַיָּה — that she gives life to her offspring, as you would say מֶה הֹוֶה לָאָדָם (Ecclesiastes 2) — in the past tense."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:26.921267829Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}